id: prefer-query-object-syntax
title: Prefer object syntax for useQuery
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can use "},{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/query/v4/docs/reference/useQuery","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"}]},{"type":"text","value":" in two different ways."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Standard"}]},{"type":"code","value":"useQuery(queryKey, queryFn?, options?)\n\n// or\n\nuseQuery(options)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This rule prefers the second option, as it is more consistent with other React Query hooks, like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQueries"},{"type":"text","value":". It will also be the only available option in a future major version."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rule-details","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rule Details"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples of "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"incorrect"}]},{"type":"text","value":" code for this rule:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-object-syntax\": \"error\" */\n\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';\n\nuseQuery(queryKey, queryFn, {\n  onSuccess,\n});\n\nuseQuery(queryKey, {\n  queryFn,\n  onSuccess,\n});","lang":"js"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples of "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"correct"}]},{"type":"text","value":" code for this rule:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';\n\nuseQuery({\n  queryKey,\n  queryFn,\n  onSuccess,\n});","lang":"js"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"when-not-to-use-it","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When Not To Use It"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you don't care about useQuery consistency, then you will not need this rule."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"attributes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attributes"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅ Recommended"}]}],"checked":true},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"🔧 Fixable"}]}],"checked":true}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"credits","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Credits"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This rule was initially developed by "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/KubaJastrz","children":[{"type":"text","value":"KubaJastrz"}]},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/KubaJastrz/eslint-plugin-react-query","children":[{"type":"text","value":"eslint-plugin-react-query"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"rule-details","text":"Rule Details","level":2},{"id":"when-not-to-use-it","text":"When Not To Use It","level":2},{"id":"attributes","text":"Attributes","level":2},{"id":"credits","text":"Credits","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou can use [`useQuery`](https://tanstack.com/query/v4/docs/reference/useQuery) in two different ways.\n\nStandard\n\n```tsx\nuseQuery(queryKey, queryFn?, options?)\n\n// or\n\nuseQuery(options)\n```\n\nThis rule prefers the second option, as it is more consistent with other React Query hooks, like `useQueries`. It will also be the only available option in a future major version.\n\n## Rule Details\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```js\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-object-syntax\": \"error\" */\n\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';\n\nuseQuery(queryKey, queryFn, {\n  onSuccess,\n});\n\nuseQuery(queryKey, {\n  queryFn,\n  onSuccess,\n});\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```js\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';\n\nuseQuery({\n  queryKey,\n  queryFn,\n  onSuccess,\n});\n```\n\n## When Not To Use It\n\nIf you don't care about useQuery consistency, then you will not need this rule.\n\n## Attributes\n\n- [x] ✅ Recommended\n- [x] 🔧 Fixable\n\n## Credits\n\nThis rule was initially developed by [KubaJastrz](https://github.com/KubaJastrz) in [eslint-plugin-react-query](https://github.com/KubaJastrz/eslint-plugin-react-query).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: prefer-query-object-syntax\ntitle: Prefer object syntax for useQuery\n---\n\nYou can use [`useQuery`](https://tanstack.com/query/v4/docs/reference/useQuery) in two different ways.\n\nStandard\n\n```tsx\nuseQuery(queryKey, queryFn?, options?)\n\n// or\n\nuseQuery(options)\n```\n\nThis rule prefers the second option, as it is more consistent with other React Query hooks, like `useQueries`. It will also be the only available option in a future major version.\n\n## Rule Details\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```js\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/prefer-query-object-syntax\": \"error\" */\n\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';\n\nuseQuery(queryKey, queryFn, {\n  onSuccess,\n});\n\nuseQuery(queryKey, {\n  queryFn,\n  onSuccess,\n});\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```js\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';\n\nuseQuery({\n  queryKey,\n  queryFn,\n  onSuccess,\n});\n```\n\n## When Not To Use It\n\nIf you don't care about useQuery consistency, then you will not need this rule.\n\n## Attributes\n\n- [x] ✅ Recommended\n- [x] 🔧 Fixable\n\n## Credits\n\nThis rule was initially developed by [KubaJastrz](https://github.com/KubaJastrz) in [eslint-plugin-react-query](https://github.com/KubaJastrz/eslint-plugin-react-query).\n"}
